<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημιουργ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a craftsman,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					248e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Prt.</u>
					322d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεχνήματα</span>
			<i>craftsmen's</i> works, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				846d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμαί,</span> of cooks,
				Clidem.<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				<i>in a workmanlike manner,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					429
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>creative,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Numen.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				11.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρακτύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					20p.466M.
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴτια, δυνάμεις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Myst.</u>
				5.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phlp.
					<u>in Mete.</u>
					12.25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κόν, τό,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρικόν</span>
			(as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐσιοποιόν</span> to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰδοποιόν</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				157
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				184
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Syrian.
					<u>in Metaph.</u>
					82.31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for the magistrates,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				<i>the official class,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1291a34
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
